## Visual concept used

A **portrait "complete dual-rail engine board"** — a new sub-archetype inside the locked Neural Signal Schematic style, deliberately distinct from 4.0's vertical escalation power-supply, 4.2's six-channel overdrive console, and 4.3's swap patch-bay. It is the fully-wired build-out of the single empty base rail 4.0 only promised.

Two power rails run the full height as the left/right spine. The **left STRUCTURAL RAIL** (`ALWAYS ON · 7 DAYS`, sub-captioned *builds the hardware: membranes · mood · new wiring*, tagged `NO SWITCH`) is a thick, steadily-glowing cyan bus. The **right STIMULANT RAIL** (`SWITCHED · 4–5 DAYS`) carries a prominent mid-throw **HEAVY-DAY master switch** (OUTPUT vs REST positions) with a ghosted dim duplicate rail behind it (`REST DAY → rail goes dark`) and an amber tag (`reset tolerance · clear huperzine · stretch the bottles`).

Between the rails, the **six act blocks** stack top→bottom in the article's bio-circuit order — I FUEL & POWER (creatine/ALCAR structural-fed, tyrosine SWITCHED), II WIRING / THE KENNEDY TRINITY (uridine+CDP-choline+DHA converging into a phosphatidylcholine→membrane node, `ALL THREE REQUIRED`, Bacopa slow-charge cell), III LOGISTICS (ginkgo widening-pipe vasodilator, amber *modest evidence — a low-risk aid, not a hero*), IV SPARK + REGULATOR (caffeine raw spike → L-theanine snubber → smooth wave, with the `2:1 THEANINE : CAFFEINE — the whole trick` callout), V ACETYLCHOLINE GUARD (alpha-GPC fuel + huperzine one-way valve), and VI MOOD & NEUROGENESIS (saffron reuptake clamp + Lion's Mane BDNF/NGF node, *real extract only — not biomass*). Each block is fed by a tap from whichever rail it belongs to, making the two-tier split visible. All converge into an `OUTPUT BUS → THE PRODUCE WINDOW` node.

The **load-bearing reveal** is the cost-inversion current meters: a bright high-draw `STRUCTURAL ≈ RM 200/mo · the bulk` bar over a thin low-draw `STIMULANT ≈ RM 80/mo · lasts ~a year` bar, beside a dim-grey reversed `WHAT YOU EXPECTED (now inverted)` ghost, capped by the caption `THE SMART-DRUG HALF IS THE CHEAP HALF.` A **rejected pre-made pre-blend inset** (amber, dashed) shows the ganged-slider trap: dragging the herbs up forces caffeine into a ~300 mg over-dose. The footer **Golden Rule** strip shows twelve trimmer pots all at a modest ~⅓ detent vs one lone slammed/clipped fader, under `A DOZEN MODEST DIALS BEAT ONE SLAMMED FADER.` Thesis lockup: `BUILD THE ENGINE. KEEP THE STRUCTURAL RAIL LIT.`

The **one red object** is the Act V cholinergic-overload interlock (`fuel + brake + DMAE driven at once → jaw clench · fog · depressive dip`, with `cycle huperzine — weekdays on, weekends off`). Every other caution (rest-day tag, ginkgo modest-evidence note, the pre-made trap) is amber, per the one-red-per-poster discipline.

